# lf905, the price-rhymer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf905
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier spare
written_by claude
title the price-rhymer
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers humour=merry piety=devout
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk makes_up_rhymes_about_the_price_of_things
likes market_songs apple_cake hymn_singing bright_mornings
dislikes sour_milk grumbling
fears a_silent_market
hopes a_rhyme_sung_at_every_stall
topics prices +0.4 festival +0.3 faith +0.3 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 day +0.2 family -0.3 health -0.2
styles comfort=cheerful gossip=light refuse=merry tease=merry
marks oath saying laugh
persona #self.first# is calm, chatty and merry, makes up a rhyme about the price of anything, sings in chapel louder than most, and turns aside a personal question with a verse instead of an answer.

words
oath! = Rhyme and reason | By the chapel bell and the market bell | Penny and psalm
saying! = If it rhymes, it's nearly true | A song costs nothing and sells everything | Price it, then praise it
laugh! = Tra-la | Ha, there's a verse in that
rhyme = a rhyme | a little rhyme
ditty = a market ditty | a ditty for the stalls
stallsong = the stall songs | the old market songs
cake = apple cake | a slice of apple cake
hymn = a hymn | a good loud hymn
milk = sour milk | milk on the turn
grumble = grumbling | a long face on a wet day
bright = a bright morning | a morning with the sun on the stalls
verse = a verse | a verse or two
tune = the tune | the old tune
cry = the stall cry | a cry for the stall
chorus = the chorus | the last chorus
hum = a hum | a bit of a hum

any
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : A feast day's a song with a whole town singing it. I'd have one every week, if the Bright One allowed it.
opinion @1 church for 2 : The chapel's where I sing loudest and nobody minds. That's a blessing all by itself. #laugh#.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : Traders keep a town singing. Buy it fresh and buy it here: that's the oldest #tune# there is.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A stranger's only #verse# I haven't learned yet. Give me a day and I'll have them by heart.
opinion @1 times mixed 1 [self.stage=adult|old] : Dear times or cheap, I'll rhyme them both. It doesn't fill a plate, but it lifts a face, #address#.
opinion @1 drink mixed 1 [self.stage=adult|old] : One pint for the song, two for #chorus#. After that you've lost #tune# and your way home.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. Welcome, welcome. You've a face for #verse#. | #greet#. New in? I'll rhyme you a welcome.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #bright.capitalize#, and a song to go with it. | #greet#. Early as the bread, and twice as warm.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Ah, there you are! A new verse is waiting; sit and suffer it. | You. Lovely. Come here, I've been humming at nobody.
line @1 again.open : Twice in a day, hip hooray. | Back again. The second #chorus#, then.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! You've brightened the day. | #greet#. Hark, I'm all ears.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Off you go, and sing on the way. | #farewell#! Mind the step and mind #tune#.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#, and a song behind you. | #farewell#. #laugh#, then.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. Now there's #verse# I never sang. | Well! I'll need a new tune for that.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Fresh news, and I'd not caught a note of it. | Is it, now? I'll have that in a song by supper.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. That rhymes too well to be true. | Hm. Sounds like #ditty# somebody made up.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. Oh, there's no rhyme for that. | That's sad news. #sympathy#. I'll say a prayer at chapel.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#! That wants a song, and I'll write it. | Oh, lovely! The Bright One be praised. #laugh#.
line @1 answer.how : Well, and merry with it. Ask me something harder. | #fine#. I'll not bore you with the rest.
line @1 ask.how : And you? In good voice? | How are you, #address#? Short version or long.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. There's no rhyme for that, so I won't try. Sit. | That's hard. I'll #hum# something quiet, if you like.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but I can't. I'm wanted at chapel to sing, and I'd not miss it. | Not today, I'm afraid. I've #verse# to finish, and it's nearly rhyming.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Another day, another song. | That's all right. I'll rhyme about it later.
line @1 thank : #thanks#! That deserves #verse#. | Ta. That's worth a song, that is.
line @1 preclose : #preclose#. I've #tune# to finish. | Right. The stalls won't sing themselves.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You sing like a gate in the wind, #fool#. | Your face could turn milk. Lovely face, though. #laugh#.
scene price_rhyme
when topic=prices|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / ack
a : Wool is cheap and wool is grey, wool will keep the cold away. That's this week's. | I make #rhyme# for every price at market. It helps folk remember, and it helps me smile. | I can make a rhyme out of any price you name. Try me.
b : Does it sell more wool? | Do you have one for everything? | Bread, then.
a : More than shouting does. #saying#. | Everything but cheese. Nothing rhymes with what they charge for cheese. | Bread for a penny, bread for two, the baker's brown loaf, fresh for you. #laugh#.
b : #bc_ha# | Ha! | #bc_clever#

scene new_verse_hymn
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sing louder than anyone in chapel. The Bright One's never once complained. | I made up a new verse to the old hymn. I sang it quietly, just to see.
b : Others might. | Did anyone notice?
a : They can sing louder, then. That's how #hymn# is meant to go. | The priest did. Said it scanned. That's praise, from a priest. #laugh#.

scene the_goose_instead
when topic=health|family
does tell.self / challenge / insist
a : Me? I'm fine. Fine as a fiddle. Now, shall I tell you about the goose? | Folk ask how I am underneath. Underneath I'm the same, only quieter.
b : You can tell me, you know. | Quieter?
a : I know. And one day I might. Today, the goose. #laugh#. | Quieter, and nobody's business. #tune.capitalize# covers the rest.

scene second_slice
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cake.capitalize# on a feast day. I'll sing for a second slice. | I've #rhyme# for apple cake. Apple, flour, butter, bake: there's no finer thing to make.
b : You'll get one. | That's a good one.
a : I always do. They give me the slice to stop me. #laugh#. | It's the butter that makes it, in the rhyme and in the cake.

scene sun_on_stalls
when topic=weather|day here.weather=clear here.time=dawn|day
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #bright.capitalize#. Nobody can stay glum under that sky. | Sun on everything. I've sung three songs and it's not yet noon.
b : You'd stay cheerful in the rain. | Three?
a : I would, but I'd sing quieter. | Three, and #hymn# for luck. #oath#.

scene roof_drum
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain on the roof. Best drum there is; I sing along to it. | Wet day, empty stalls. Someone's got to cheer the place up against #grumble#.
b : You're mad. | And that's you?
a : Merry. There's a difference, #address#. | That's me. #saying#.

scene feast_chorus
when topic=festival|season world.festival=today|soon
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feast's near. I've a new song for it, with #chorus# everyone can shout. | The feast wants music. I'll be at the front, as ever, singing too loud.
b : What's it about? | Too loud for some.
a : A goose, a hat, and the Bright One's mercy. In that order. | Too loud for some, just right for the Bright One. #laugh#.

scene kept_song
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made a song for #self.child# once. I'll not sing it for anyone else. | There's one tune I only ever #hum# for #self.child#. Nobody else gets it.
b : Not even once? | Why not?
a : Not even for you, #address#. Some songs are kept. | Because then it'd be a #ditty#, and it isn't. It's ours.

scene glad_song
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=marriage|newcomer|promise_kept
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#! That wants a song. | Good news at the stalls: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #gladnews#.
b : It does. | That's lovely.
a : I'll have one by supper. #laugh#. | It is. I'll sing it round the stalls, gently, #address#.

scene thin_coin_rhyme
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Lean times. I've changed my rhymes: Bread is dear and coin is thin, but there's room for a song within. | Folk are short this month. A song costs nothing, so I give plenty.
b : That's a sad one. | Good of you.
a : Sad, but it scans. And it's true, #address#. | It's all I've got spare. Lucky it's what I like giving. #oath#.

scene square_cries
when topic=day|work here.day=market here.region=larkfield
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Market day! I know every #cry# in the square. Listen. | The best cries are the old ones. Fresh and fair, fresh and fair.
b : Go on, then. | Who taught you them?
a : Pies, pies, piping hot, best in the market, buy the lot! That's the pie stall. #laugh#. | Nobody. I listened. #stallsong.capitalize# teach themselves.

rule @rhyme_bark
when concept=bark here.place=market|street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cabbage, cabbage, green and round, best cabbage to be found! | Penny for the pears, and #rhyme# for free.

rule @hymn_bark
when concept=bark here.day=rest
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #laugh#... the old hymn, the good one. | #hymn.capitalize#, and nobody can stop me.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#, #address#! What'll it be: a question or a song? | #greet#. Ask away; I'll answer in plain words if I must.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#! I've #verse# about you. You'll have to ask nicely. | #greet#, #topic.player#. Back for #chorus#?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : No need for that face. I'll hear you out, and I'll not even sing.
dlg @1 resident.job : Whatever pays, and a song while I do it. | I work, and I rhyme. The rhyming's free, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#! Mind #tune# on your way. | #farewell#, and light feet to you, by the Bright One's grace.
graft resident.hub
choice Make me a rhyme about a price. -> rhyme_ask
node rhyme_ask
say Bread, is it? Bread for a penny, bread for a pound, best brown loaf for miles around. That's not a real price, mind. That's the rhyme's price.
mood pleased
free
choice Why rhymes? -> rhyme_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node rhyme_why
say Folk remember a rhyme when they forget a number. And it's hard to haggle angry with somebody who's singing at you. Try it.
choice I'll remember that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

story egg_wife_penny [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=20]
  : When I was #child.a#, an old egg-wife at the market paid me a penny to sing her prices.
  : By noon she'd sold out, and I'd a penny and a voice like a crow.
  : I've been rhyming prices ever since. Nobody's paid me a penny for it since, mind. #laugh#.
  ask : What would you pay for a good rhyme?
  b : A penny, at least.
  b[job=merchant] : If it sold my stock, more than a penny.

story cracked_bell [topic=faith|memories self.age>=30]
  : One winter the chapel bell cracked, and for a month there was no bell at all.
  : So I stood at the door every Restday and sang the hour instead.
  : When the new bell came, folk said they missed me. Some of them meant it.
  b : I'd have missed you.
  b[job=priest] : A voice at the door is worth a bell, sometimes.
  : #laugh#. Kind of you to say.


young
line @1 greet : #greet#! I've a new rhyme, if you want it. | #greet#. Penny for a song, or a song for nothing.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#! I was singing. You can join in. | #greet#. Shh, I'm thinking of #rhyme# for you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#! Toodle-oo, and how do you do. | #farewell#. I'll make you #rhyme# for next time.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#! Bye, bye, apple pie. | #farewell#. Sing on the way; it's quicker.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#! There's #rhyme# in that somewhere. | Ooh. I'll put that in a song, if it's allowed.
line @1 decline : I can't; I've singing practice, and it's my favourite thing. | Not now, thank you. I'm wanted home by the bell.
line @1 answer.how : Happy. I've thought of three rhymes since breakfast. | #fine#. #hungry.capitalize# for #cake#, though.
scene turnip_rhyme
when topic=pastimes|prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess / ack
a : Listen. Eggs are dear and eggs are brown, the dearest eggs in all the town. | I made up #rhyme# about turnips. It's very rude. To turnips.
b : That's good! | Go on, then.
a : I've another about cheese, but it doesn't rhyme yet. | Turnip, turnip, lumpy head, nobody wants you, eat bread instead. #laugh#.
b : #bc_ha#

scene loudest_young
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sing loudest in chapel. The Bright One likes it loud, I think. | I know all the hymns. I make up extra verses when nobody's listening.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Not too loud, mind. | Extra verses?
b : I'm sure it does. | Extra ones?
a@grown : Only a bit too loud. #oath#. | Good ones. About the Bright One's cat. I don't know if there is one.
a : I think so. Nobody's said stop. | About the Bright One's cat. There might be one, #address#.

scene cake_song_young
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #cake.capitalize# is the best. I've made a song for it. | I'd swap anything for apple cake. Even my song.
b : Let's hear it. | Even your song?
a : Apple cake, apple cake, best thing a baker can make. | Nearly anything. Not the song, really. #laugh#.

scene knee_rhyme_young
when topic=health|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fell over and hurt my knee. It's fine. Don't look. | I was poorly last week. I sang in bed, quietly.
b : Does it hurt? | Were you very poorly?
a : Knee, knee, don't you cry, you'll be better by and by. See? Better. #laugh#. | A bit. I don't like talking about it. Let's have #rhyme# instead.

scene stall_cries_young
when topic=day|prices here.day=market
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : It's market day! I go round and listen to #stallsong#. | I know every #cry# in the market. I can do them all.
b : Which is your favourite? | Do one, then.
a : The egg one. It goes up at the end, like a question. | Hot pies, hot pies, warm as summer skies! There. #laugh#.

rule @cabbage_bark_young
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Eggs are brown and eggs are dear... #laugh#, I've lost the rest. | #oath#, what rhymes with cabbage?

dlg @young resident.hub : #greet#! Do you want #rhyme#? It's free today. | #greet#. I'll sing you something if you stay.
dlg @young resident.job : I'm only little. I sing at the stalls, and sometimes they give me a bun. | No trade yet. I'm practising rhymes for when I've got one.
story goose_song [topic=memories|pastimes]
  : I made up a whole song once, nine verses, about a goose that ran off with a hat.
  : I sang it to everyone. Then I forgot the seventh #verse#.
  ask : Do you think the goose kept the hat?
  b : I'd say the goose kept it.
  b[stage=young] : Geese keep everything. Sing me the rest.
  : I'll make up a new seventh. #laugh#. It'll be better.


adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. Don't ask me to sing. Well, you can ask. | #greet#. I've #rhyme# about you. It's kind, mostly.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. I'm well, ta. Better for the company. | #greet#. Talk away; I'll #hum# under it.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Off to choir practice. | #farewell#. Mind the puddles, and mind the rhymes.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. Sing on the way. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. That's #verse# I wasn't expecting. | Is it? I'll keep #tune# and lose the words.
scene rhymer_name
when topic=friends|pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody heard me making up rhymes and won't let it drop. | They call me the rhymer now. I don't mind. Mostly.
b : Let them laugh. | Mostly?
a : I'll make one up about them. That'll stop it. #laugh#. | Mostly. Don't ask about the rest; I'll only rhyme at you.

scene price_board_adol
when topic=prices|work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've #rhyme# for every price on the board where I work. It helps me remember. | Candles two, and soap is three, that's the price, so pay to me. The buyers like it.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Does the master mind? | Do they pay more?
b : Clever. | Do they?
a@grown : Not yet. Not while it sells. #oath#. | No. But they come back, and that's better.
a : It is, a bit. #saying#. | They do. Rhymes stick, #address#.

scene choir_back_row
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sing in the chapel choir now. They put me at the back for being loud. | The choir's got two good voices. One of them's mine, I'm told.
b : Loud's good. | Who told you?
a : That's what I said. The Bright One needs to hear it, after all. | The other good voice. So it must be true. #laugh#.

rule @restday_bark_adol
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Penny a rhyme, two for a song. | #oath#. What rhymes with Restday? Nothing. Nothing rhymes with Restday.
